          "returnType": "LoaderScope",
          "description": "Creates an independent child claim owner under a live parent. Destroying the child releases only its claims. Destroying the parent releases its current children first. Names are diagnostic labels and do not identify or reuse a scope. Call this only before parent teardown. Unlike get(), load(), and loadContainer(), this revision does not reject creation after destruction; that late child must be explicitly destroyed by its caller."
        },
        {
          "name": "destroy",
          "signature": "destroy(): void",
          "signatureTokens": [
            {
              "text": "destroy",
              "kind": "name"
            },
            {
              "text": "(",
              "kind": "punctuation"
            },
            {
              "text": ")",
              "kind": "punctuation"
            },
            {
              "text": ": ",
              "kind": "punctuation"
            },
            {
              "text": "void",
              "kind": "keyword"
            }
          ],
          "params": [],
          "returnType": "void",
          "description": "Releases every claim this scope still holds and destroys any child scope it still has. Assets another scope also holds stay resident, and destroying an already-destroyed scope is a no-op. Acquiring through the scope afterwards - get, load, loadContainer - throws, because the claim it would register has no owner left to release it."
        },
